.TH SPACEGL-CLIENT 1 "2026-04-19" "SpaceGL @VERSION@" "SpaceGL Manual"
.SH NAME
spacegl-client \- SpaceGL tactical bridge launcher script
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spacegl-client
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ gl | vk ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B spacegl-client
is a Bash wrapper script that provides an interactive startup interface
for the SpaceGL game client. It displays the SpaceGL banner, asks for
the master key interactively when the
.B SPACEGL_KEY
environment variable is not already set, and then delegates execution
to
.BR spacegl_client (1).
.PP
All arguments passed to this script are forwarded verbatim to the
underlying
.B spacegl_client
binary. Pass
.B gl
to use the OpenGL frontend or
.B vk
to use the Vulkan frontend (GPU-driven rendering by default, with a
CPU-driven fallback;
.B SPACEGL_GPD=0
selects the CPU-driven path).
.PP
Server identity (wire revision 4): on the first connection to a server
the deck prints the server's fingerprint and pins its key in
.IR ~/.spacegl/known_servers .
Check it against the fingerprint the server prints at boot. A later
connection to the same address with another key is refused with
"SERVER IDENTITY CHANGED"; if the change is legitimate (the server's data
directory was replaced), remove that server's line from the file.
.SH OPTIONS
Any option accepted by
.BR spacegl_client (1)
is passed through unchanged.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SPACEGL_KEY
If set, the authentication key prompt is skipped and this value is used directly.
.TP
.B SPACEGL_SERVER_KEY
The server's identity key (64 hex digits, from
.BR "spacegl-server \-\-print\-identity" ):
the deck accepts only a server that signs the handshake with it.
.TP
.B SPACEGL_KNOWN_SERVERS
Path of the known_servers file (default ~/.spacegl/known_servers).
.TP
.B SPACEGL_GPD
For the Vulkan frontend: unset or 1 GPU-driven (default), 0 CPU-driven.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.spacegl/known_servers
The pinned identity of every server this deck has met.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR spacegl_client (1),
.BR spacegl-server (1),
.BR spacegl_server (1),
.BR spacegl_vulkan (1),
.BR spacegl_3dview (1)
